    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0341" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10508: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase—Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-09T18:00:00+08:00">July 9, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 9—10:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>552.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs, C. T. Wang, is expected here tomorrow,
                    presumably to discuss the Manchurian situation with Chiang Kai-shek<anchor
                        n="73" xml:id="d90-f1"/> and Marshal Chang Hsüeh-liang.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d90-f1" n="73" xml:id="d90-f1-content">
                <p>Chairman of the State Council of the National Government of the Republic of
                    China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
